DESCRIPTION:MSCA09|Forum|Virtual\nLanguage: English\nTopic: Accessibility\n
 IMG: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lwBN4TApXAAsV7XLBeSOsRgBSrZwJHTA/view
 ?usp=sharing\nLink: NorthSouth-Remote-Communitities-English-2022.07.16 http
 s://drive.google.com/file/d/1Hg6XcrQ42LWHmdCZ0dDt7kNg36kdwRvf/view?usp=shar
 ing\nLink: NorthSouth-Remote-Communitities-Spanish-2022.07.16 https://drive
 .google.com/file/d/1GJKoJ3mp-pMOkKgnzdmNwlmJaLO_5fyt/view?usp=sharing\n--\n
 North/South Virtual Special Forum about Remote Communities\n“Beyond Languag
 e\, Culture & Geography: Sobriety Within Everybody’s Reach”\n\nREGISTRATION
  IS FREE AND NOW OPEN! (https://na.eventscloud.com/ereg/index.php?eventid=6
 88779)\n\nPlease join with us as we stretch the virtual hand of A.A. from C
 anada and the United States to the furthest reaches of South America\, on S
 aturday\, July 16\, 2022\, from 11:00am to 7:00pm New York time. (8am to 4p
 m Pacific Time.)\n\nOur Special Forum\, coordinated by the US/Canada Genera
 l Service Office\, will expand on the definition of “remote” to include the
  challenges of not just geography\, but of language and of culture. Three A
 A service structures and four countries are involved in the planning\, and 
 we welcome our friends to the south\, Argentina and Chile\, as partners in 
 the project.\n\nThe use of virtual technology is allowing us an unprecedent
 ed opportunity to share with our fellow members in a very profound way. We 
 look forward to joining with you in extending the hand of AA up and down th
 e shared degree of latitude between the north and south.\n\nEnglish Flyer: 
 NorthSouth-Remote-Communitities-English-2022.07.16\nSpanish Flyer: NorthSou
 th-Remote-Communitities-Spanish-2022.07.16
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T022541Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:North/South Connections Virtual Special Forum – A.A. in Remote Comm
 unities
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
